  "id": "s09-breaks-zones-limits",
  "title": "Breaks, priority zones and daily load limits (D9b)",
  "notes": [
    "Issue #70, D9b (legacy-parity-inventory.md PAR-013, PAR-077, PAR-078; SQL case 140). One plan with two periods (3 days x 3 slots), one per specialty, so that the period-wide metrics of each run are its own.",
    "Legacy side: the zones through the legacy zone editor (get_form_edit_zpriori, then custom_set_zpriori with every cell, as ancoragoh_client_forms_zpriori.js posts it); breaks and limits, which no screen wrote (A-4), through the generated add_Receso and add_HigieneParaProfesor / _Brigada handlers. Drupal side: PeriodInputs, the save of the editors.",
    "Specialty E: teacher TA has a daily load limit of 1 and cohort B2 one of 0, which change the placements of run E (default options). Specialty F: its activity type C2 has priority zones, and run F uses parche1, the only option with which the zones change the cells. A break after slot 1 of Week changes only hours; the receso row itself is compared. Teacher TS has a restricted cell in Week F."
  ],
